dbus_manager: no dbus_fast import without a system bus

Kiln OS runs no dbus-daemon, so there is no system bus socket. Moonraker
imported dbus_fast (2.6 MB of Python and Cython modules on the AD5X)
for its dbus_manager core component at every start, tried to connect
and logged "Unable to Connect to D-Bus". Nothing on Kiln OS uses the
bus: the machine component runs the kiln_agent provider (patch 0006),
not systemd_dbus, and system updates through PackageKit are off.

dbus_manager now reads the system bus address as dbus_fast does
(DBUS_SYSTEM_BUS_ADDRESS, else unix:path=/var/run/dbus/system_bus_socket).
When every entry is a unix socket path that doesn't exist it imports
nothing from dbus_fast, connects to nothing and logs one line. Its API
stays: is_connected() is False, get_interface()/get_interfaces() raise
"Bus not available", check_permission() warns and returns False, as
upstream does after a failed connection; DbusError is an exception
class that is never raised, so "except dbus_mgr.DbusError" in callers
still works. With a bus socket (or another transport) dbus_fast is
imported and used as before.

Upstream: not submitted (AD5X open OS)

